diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index ffc07e0..b1bd2a4 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -52,3 +52,76 @@ avatars, broadcasts, and push notifications exactly as humans do.
 `MessagesController#set_room` was extended to resolve top-level
 `/messages/:id` (from the bot `Location`) via `reachable_messages`, keeping
 nested `/rooms/:room_id/messages/:id` unchanged.
+
+## Webhooks (bot mentions)
+
+Bots may have an optional `webhook_url` (`users.webhook_url`, `Bot`-only):
+
+- `BotsController#bot_params` permits `:webhook_url`; `_form` (shared by
+  `/bots/new` and `/bots/:id/edit`) has a `url_field` labelled "Webhook URL"
+  (label + placeholder + `aria-label`, optional).
+- `Bot#normalize_webhook_url` strips and nilifies blank, so saving with an
+  empty field removes the webhook. `Bot#webhook_url_must_be_valid_http_url`
+  requires `http(s)` with a host when present (allows `localhost`/private
+  IPs for self-hosted bots and QA harnesses).
+
+Bots appear in `@`-mention autocomplete like people:
+
+- `Autocompletable::UsersController` already scopes to `room.users` (or
+  `User.all`) with `active`, which includes `Bot` STI rows. Bots auto-join
+  open rooms via `grant_membership_to_open_rooms`, so they show up in open
+  rooms without extra steps; closed rooms list bots in the member UI so they
+  can be added like people.
+- `lib/rails_ext/action_text_attachables.rb` now permits `Bot` in
+  `ATTACHABLES_PERMITTED_WITH_INVALID_SIGNATURES` (alongside `User`) so
+  expired SGIDs still resolve for bots.
+
+Mention delivery is async so posting never waits on bot HTTP:
+
+- `Message::Mentionee#mentioned_bots` finds `Bot.active` with a webhook among
+  the message's `attachables.grep(Bot)` (permissive: works even if the bot
+  isn't yet a member, unlike `mentionees` which filters to `room.users`).
+- `Room#receive` (called via `after_create_commit`) now also calls
+  `notify_bots_later`, which does `Bot::MentionJob.perform_later(bot, message)`
+  once per mentioned webhook bot. No `Net::HTTP` in the request path.
+- `Bot::MentionJob` (`app/jobs/bot/mention_job.rb`):
+  - `discard_on ActiveJob::DeserializationError`; rescues and logs all
+    network/format errors without retry storms.
+  - `ensure_bot_membership` via `find_or_create_by` so `reply_to` (which
+    requires membership in `Bots::MessagesController`) works even for bots
+    mentioned before being added.
+  - POSTs `Content-Type: application/json` to `bot.webhook_url` with:
+    ```json
+    {
+      "event": "mention",
+      "author": { "id": 7, "name": "Alice" },
+      "room":   { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/<bot_code>/messages" },
+      "message": {
+        "id": 118,
+        "body": { "text": "stripped plain", "html": "<div>…full rich-text…</div>" },
+        "link": "/rooms/5/@118"
+      }
+    }
+    ```
+    - `text` is `plain_text_body` with the bot's own `"@#{name}"` stripped
+      (`gsub` + `strip` + collapse spaces, preserving newlines); each bot
+      gets its own stripped view when several are mentioned.
+    - `html` is `message.body.body.to_html` (full Trix HTML, `<div>` when
+      from the composer).
+    - `reply_to` is `bot_room_messages_path(room_id:, bot_code:)` (the bot's
+      own posting URL for that room); `link` is `room_at_message_path`.
+      Both relative; the bot knows its Campfire origin.
+  - Handles the sync reply:
+    - `200` with `text/plain` or `text/html` (charset-tolerant via
+      `response.content_type`) → `room.messages.create!(body:, creator: bot)`
+      + `broadcast_create` (same as the bot POST API). Blank bodies ignored.
+    - `204` → no message. Any other status/content-type → ignored + logged.
+  - Timeouts (`open 5s`, `read/write 10s`), `Accept: text/plain, text/html`,
+    and basic-auth from `userinfo` in the URL are supported. No
+    `PrivateNetworkGuard` pinning, so `127.0.0.1`/`localhost` webhooks work.
+  - Async replies use the `reply_to` URL (`POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_code/messages`,
+    raw body, `201` + `Location`), exactly as the existing bot API.
+
+Conventions kept: switches stay checkboxes, confirmations stay native
+`confirm()` (bot delete uses `data-turbo-confirm`), and the "Webhook URL"
+label is kept verbatim for QA selectors.
